  "about": "Mr. Douglas Wood is a principal software engineer at VT MÄK. Mr. Wood’s current assignment is on the Link team at MAK involved with interoperability across distributed simulation protocols. He is specifically leading the development of the Logger product which records and replays simulation data transmitted across the network.  He recently contributed to the HLA Traffic Analyzer Program as the interoperability engineer. As chief architect and lead developer of the MAK High-Performance RTI, was responsible for bringing the HLA 1.3 MÄK RTI from a partial implementation to a DoD verified RTI and for the transition of the RTI to the IEEE 1516 HLA Specification. Mr. Wood was the principal investigator on the Air Force SBIR “An Optimized HLA Environment”.  In this role, he led the research and development of RTI features to reduce latency and bandwidth. Previously, Mr. Wood created the FOM Mapper Builder, a graphical user interface that automatically generates Federation Object Model mapping code for MÄK’s VR-Link networking toolkit.\n\nMr. Wood has over twenty three years of experience in simulation and training.  He has performed and managed research and software development in distributed simulation architectures and protocols, automated behavior, electronic warfare simulation, emergency management simulation, and training device databases.\n\nSpecialties: Software architecture and development",
